{"kind":"assert","text":"Correction to review 61a8c0ce: the diagnosis allowlist did not hold for every thrown value\n\nMy approval said that a report holds \"an allowlisted error name\". At 7d74234c that is wrong for a thrown value with a stateful `name` getter. `diag.ts` checks one read of `thrown.name` and returns a second read, so the second value can be text outside the list. I read that line during the review and missed this. The builder's finding acc45396 is correct.\n\nThe code predates this head, and no leak has been observed. The other conclusions of 61a8c0ce stand for the bytes they covered, and the lineage predicate is unaffected.\n\nUnder ruling 46552b89 I will review the diff from 7d74234c and the new gate when the head returns. On first reading, the repair at f0ab0153 has the right form: it reads the name once, then checks and returns that same value.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:61a8c0cefb16938d68c231779d3169eef2c1ca93 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:070231aadcb17348891458bc2eedb5bbf529860c, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:364be032963705e2746eb41a8fd37b232d456fb4, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4aa3a00525fb9f500e2c9640ccab369106838cf1, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:96416841dead2e1a55f7797fae0ea7c6e8ea8c8c and 2 more","to":"planner"}}